  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi recently spoke at Columbia University in the United States, where he characterized the Indian economy as being on the verge of a crisis. This assessment has triggered a sharp reaction from the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and its allies. Party officials and representatives, including Diya Kumari, criticized Mr. Gandhi for allegedly tarnishing India's image internationally. The BJP described the comments as propaganda, while a spokesperson for the Janata Dal (United) (JD(U)), Rajeev Ranjan Prasad, countered the claims by noting that India's economic growth performance is currently stronger than the global rate. The debate highlights ongoing tensions regarding how domestic political figures address national issues while on foreign platforms, with government supporters crediting current diplomatic and economic policies for strengthening the country's status on the world stage.",
